<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section__head"><h2>From application to winner</h2>
  <p>Entries are application based, evidence based and jury evaluated.</p></div>
  <ol class="steps"><li class="step"><h3>Choose your categories</h3><p>Pick every category that fits your business.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Apply</h3><p>Send details about your company and the service you are entering.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Add evidence</h3><p>Upload the data, screenshots and results that support your application.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Eligibility check</h3><p>The AirStars team confirms that your entry fits the category.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Jury evaluation</h3><p>Jurors evaluate your entry against the published criteria.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Shortlist</h3><p>The strongest entries in each category go forward.</p></li><li class="step"><h3>Finalists</h3><p>Finalists are announced for each category.</p></li><li class="step step--last"><h3>Winner</h3><p>One winner is named in each category.</p></li></ol>
  <p class="note-line"><a href="/how-it-works/">Read the full process and key dates</a></p>
</div></section>

<section class="section section--panel"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section__head"><h2>What the jury looks at</h2>
  <p>Ten areas apply to every entry. Each family adds its own points.</p></div>
  <dl class="criteria"><div><dt>How the service is presented</dt><dd>How clearly the company explains what travellers get, where and at what price.</dd></div><div><dt>How it is sold</dt><dd>The sales channels, the buying journey and how easy it is to say yes.</dd></div><div><dt>How reservations are managed</dt><dd>Confirmation, changes, cancellations and what happens after booking.</dd></div><div><dt>Range and coverage</dt><dd>How many airports, lounges and services travellers can reach through the company.</dd></div><div><dt>User experience</dt><dd>How the product feels to use, on any device, for first-time and repeat customers.</dd></div><div><dt>Customer satisfaction</dt><dd>What customers say and what the company measures.</dd></div><div><dt>Sales performance</dt><dd>Results over the entry period, shown with evidence.</dd></div><div><dt>Service variety</dt><dd>The mix of services offered and how well they work together.</dd></div><div><dt>Technology infrastructure</dt><dd>The systems behind the service and how reliably they perform.</dd></div><div><dt>After-sales support</dt><dd>How the company helps travellers when something needs fixing.</dd></div></dl>
  <p class="note-line"><a href="/judging/">How entries are judged</a></p>
</div></section>

